From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:49:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] shaders: fog distance without overflow on mediump-only
 GPUs

The fog in the node, object and cloud fragment shaders used
length(eyeVec) / fogDistance. Where the fragment shader has no highp
(GLES 2.0 without GL_FRAGMENT_PRECISION_HIGH, e.g. Mali-400 with Mesa
lima, which is fp16), Luanti declares mediump and defines highp away, so
length() squares eye-space coordinates in fp16. Beyond ~256 units
(sqrt(65504), 25.6 nodes) the sum overflows to infinity, the clarity
drops to 0 and every pixel farther than that is painted with the fog
color: a sphere of ~25 nodes around the camera, whatever viewing_range
is. By day it melts into the sky; at night distant terrain shows as
flat silhouettes.

length(eyeVec / fogDistance) is the same value and stays near 1.

Upstream: not sent yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/client/shaders/cloud_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl b/client/shaders/cloud_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
index edbcd60b6..34cc7cfb4 100644
--- a/client/shaders/cloud_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
+++ b/client/shaders/cloud_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ void main(void)
 	vec4 col = varColor;
 
 	float clarity = clamp(fogShadingParameter
-		- fogShadingParameter * length(eyeVec) / fogDistance, 0.0, 1.0);
+		- fogShadingParameter * length(eyeVec / fogDistance), 0.0, 1.0);
 	col.rgb = mix(fogColor.rgb, col.rgb, clarity);
 
 	gl_FragColor = col;
diff --git a/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl b/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
index d8231ef26..e0d88afb4 100644
--- a/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
+++ b/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
@@ -597,7 +597,7 @@ void main(void)
 	// should be more efficient as well.
 	// Note: clarity = (1 - fogginess)
 	float clarity = clamp(fogShadingParameter
-		- fogShadingParameter * length(eyeVec) / fogDistance, 0.0, 1.0);
+		- fogShadingParameter * length(eyeVec / fogDistance), 0.0, 1.0);
 	float fogColorMax = max(max(fogColor.r, fogColor.g), fogColor.b);
 	// Prevent zero division.
 	if (fogColorMax < 0.0000001) fogColorMax = 1.0;
diff --git a/client/shaders/object_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl b/client/shaders/object_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
index 0eac9f78c..8f1f331f3 100644
--- a/client/shaders/object_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
+++ b/client/shaders/object_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
@@ -454,7 +454,7 @@ void main(void)
 	// should be more efficient as well.
 	// Note: clarity = (1 - fogginess)
 	float clarity = clamp(fogShadingParameter
-		- fogShadingParameter * length(eyeVec) / fogDistance, 0.0, 1.0);
+		- fogShadingParameter * length(eyeVec / fogDistance), 0.0, 1.0);
 	float fogColorMax = max(max(fogColor.r, fogColor.g), fogColor.b);
 	// Prevent zero division.
 	if (fogColorMax < 0.0000001) fogColorMax = 1.0;
